From 45094544c85ce8335ed54078517063b7f09a28a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): certified two-pass Cauchy-Schwarz lm_head greedy
 vocabulary screening

- Add 8-bit sign-magnitude screening table W_q (1.0 B/elem) and per-row certified Cauchy-Schwarz residual bounds (row_scale, row_bound, row_mma_tol) in vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/vocab.py (build_screen_weights), handling both in-window and extreme out-of-window pack12 exceptions.

- Replace full-vocabulary 12-bit pack12 greedy pair projection in project_head_greedy_pairs with a 6-kernel PDL-chained certified two-pass pipeline (vocab_x_norm -> vocab_screen_greedy_partials -> vocab_row_thresholds -> vocab_compact_tiles -> vocab_packed_refine_partials -> vocab_active_greedy_finish) that screens all vocabulary columns at 1.0 B/elem and refines only the < 0.3-1.8% active columns whose certified upper bound can reach the exact winning row threshold.

- Co-allocate W_q inside the single DRM dumb-buffer display carve-out allocation in PackedBf16LmHeadMethod.create_weights alongside the 12-bit packed head weight so both passes stream from the display carve-out without extra DRM allocations.

- Register the 6 new kernels in tests/kernels/deepseek_v41_pdl_sources.py and add edge-case and carve-out co-allocation unit tests in tests/kernels/quantization/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_vocab.py.
